crates/runtime/src/container/runtime.rs (the default masked and read-only paths)
    The lists of paths that the runtime masks or mounts read-only follow
    those of containers-common (pkg/config, DefaultMaskedPaths and
    DefaultReadOnlyPaths), which derive them from Moby/Docker.  They are
    lists of kernel paths and the default capability set in
    crates/runtime/src/container/caps.rs is a list of capability names; both
    are given for attribution.  License: Apache-2.0.

vendor/zlink-core
    zlink-core 0.7.1 (https://github.com/z-galaxy/zlink), the varlink
    library, with these changes: in src/unix_utils.rs a descriptor
    received over a socket is close-on-exec and a truncated control
    message is an error; in src/connection/{read,write}_connection.rs the
    trace messages no longer print the varlink messages (they carry
    registry credentials and secrets), only their direction and size; in
    src/connection/read_connection.rs the descriptors of a read go with
    the message its last byte is in, and a call is taken with either form
    of "no parameters" (`{}` or none), and a reply is read by a probe of
    its kind (its `error` member) and then as the error or the reply,
    instead of an untagged enum, with the reading of a message out of the
    generic code (and in write_connection.rs the end of a written one); in
    src/server/mod.rs a call that does not match its method is answered
    InvalidParameter before the connection is closed; in
    src/connection/{read,write}_connection.rs the buffers grow by doubling;
    in src/varlink_service/interface_description.rs a description can be
    a given text; in src/connection/{mod,read_connection,write_connection}.rs
    the sending of a call, the growth of the buffer and the trace are out
    of the generic code and the members of a reply are read before its
    parameters, so that the code of a call that depends on its type is
    its serialization and the decoding of its reply; in
    src/connection/{socket,chain/reply_stream}.rs the stream of the
    replies of a call with more is Send.
    Copyright 2025 Zeeshan Ali Khan. License: MIT.

vendor/zlink-idl
    zlink-idl 0.7.1 (https://github.com/z-galaxy/zlink), the varlink
    interface description types, with this change: src/field.rs,
    custom_object.rs, error.rs, method.rs and type/mod.rs write a record,
    an error, an inline object or the parameters of a method that have
    comments one field a line, the comments above their field, and
    src/comment.rs writes an empty comment as `#` (the parser and the
    tests of the crate are kept, three of the tests, in interface.rs and
    parse/tests.rs, expect the new layout).  Copyright 2025 Zeeshan Ali
    Khan. License: MIT.

vendor/zlink-macros
    zlink-macros 0.7.1 (https://github.com/z-galaxy/zlink), the macros of
    the varlink library, with this change: src/service/{attrs,codegen}.rs
    the attribute `description` of the service macro gives the text of the
    interface descriptions, and the generated descriptors exist only in the
    tests (the tests and the dev-dependencies of the crate are not
    vendored), and src/utils.rs the comment of a doc attribute loses the
    space that follows its `///` (it was written twice).  Copyright 2025
    Zeeshan Ali Khan. License: MIT.

vendor/tar
    tar 0.4.46 (https://github.com/composefs/tar-rs, from alexcrichton/tar-rs),
    the tar reader and writer, with these changes: in src/archive.rs and
    src/entry.rs the pieces of the map of an old GNU sparse entry are a
    VecDeque of at most 32768, and src/entry.rs has
    `Entry::take_sparse_blocks`, which drops the holes of such an entry and
    returns where its data goes (the tests, the examples and the
    dev-dependencies of the crate are not vendored).  Copyright Alex Crichton
    and the tar-rs contributors.  License: MIT OR Apache-2.0.

